# audit-ordering log — evidence that the gate was designed from the spec, not from the bytes
#
# Why this file exists (PLAN.md step 1.0 + the worker brief): the audit is only worth
# something if the gate was written from the SPEC before any tensor-data byte was read,
# because the whole point of the audit is that llama.cpp and our engine read the same bytes
# and can never witness a converter bug between them (PLAN.md §"Why an audit exists at all").
# Ordering is therefore a REPORTED FIELD, not an assumption. Rows tagged `tool:` are appended
# by tools/audit_published_quant.py itself; rows tagged `manual:` were written by hand from the
# command transcript. Times are `date -u` on this box; the box clock reads 2026-10-25 while the
# repo's document convention is 2026-10-26 (progress/2026-10-26/step1-kickoff.md §"Box clock
# note"), so both are shown wherever it matters.
