2026-10-25T01:20:39Z | manual | F0: `python3 tools/audit_published_quant.py --selftest` -> FAIL. Three of five synthetic fixtures generated ZERO elements (block-list vs flat-list mismatch in the K-quant packers), Q8_0 indices were stored with a +128 bias and read back as int8, Q5_K applied `>>4` twice on the high nibble, Q6_K took the scale index from the 32-element chunk instead of the 16-element sub-block, and the floor-honesty bound was computed from the ideal step rather than the realized one. Every one of these was the reader's own bug, caught before any file byte was judged — which is the entire argument for step 1.0.
2026-10-25T01:23:38Z | manual | F0: `--selftest` -> FAIL (Q6_K scale index still `2g+2k`, and the size guard now makes a silent empty fixture impossible).
