2026-10-25T01:43:45Z | manual | F5 (step 1.4) first data run -> FAIL: routers/norms/ssm_norm matched, everything else did not. Diagnosis (`/tmp/dbg3.py`, post-gate reads) showed the audit's V-reorder index map had the k and v axes swapped and the norm `+1` was done in f32, not bf16. Both fixed from the converter source; `v_grouped_order()` was added as an independent formulation of the reorder so the witness no longer checks the mapper against itself.
2026-10-25T01:50:21Z | manual | F5 (step 1.4): `--exact` -> FAIL with exactly one element outside: `blk.1.ssm_a` element 21 is 1 f32 ulp from `-exp(A_log)` (route `V-reorder + -exp(f32)`). A 60-digit `Decimal` exp agrees with the double route, so the file's producer computed `exp` in float32 with a non-correctly-rounded libm. Recorded as a near miss and still judged FAIL: zero tolerance, no carve-out invented here. Router rows: 3/3 bit-exact as stored.
